==Old English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|ang|mear}}, {{l|ang|mearg}}

===Etymology===
From {{proto|Germanic|marhaz|lang=ang}}, from {{proto|Indo-European|márkos|horse|lang=ang}}. Cognate with Old Frisian ''[[merie]]'', Old Saxon ''[[merge#Old Saxon|merge]]'' (Dutch ''[[merrie]]''), Old High German ''[[meriha]]'', mare (German ''[[Mähre]]''), Old Norse ''[[merr]]'', ''[[marr]]'' (Swedish ''[[märr]]'').  The Indo-European root is also the source of Irish ''[[marc#Irish|marc]]'' and Welsh ''[[march#Welsh|march]]'', horse

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/mæɑrx/|lang=ang}}

